e black chamber, where the figure is revealed to be an empty shell. As the prince dies, the plague manifests among the revelers, and one by one they perish, extinguishing the lights and silence falling over the abbey as death claims all.\"\n    28→    }\n    29→  ],\n    30→  \"characters\": [\n    31→    {\n    32→      \"id\": \"char_the_prince_prospero_d85685e9\",\n    33→      \"canonical_name\": \"the Prince Prospero\",\n    34→      \"aliases\": [\n    35→        \"the mummer\"\n    36→      ],\n    37→      \"role\": null,\n    38→      \"appearance\": null,\n    39→      \"personality\": null,\n    40→      \"voice_guidance\": null,\n    41→      \"descriptions\": [\n    42→        {\n    43→          \"text\": \"Prince Prospero is a tyrannical and self-indulgent ruler who responds to perceived threats with violent rage and authoritarian control. His actions escalate from arrogance and cruelty to panic and futile aggression, culminating in his own death at the hands of the very symbol of the plague he sought to deny. His behavior reveals a deep-seated fear of mortality and a willingness to sacrifice others to maintain power and illusion.\",\n    44→          \"source_position\": 10339,\n    45→          \"chapter_index\": null,\n    46→          \"confidence\": \"llm_refined\"\n    47→        }\n    48→      ],\n    49→      \"relationships\": {},\n    50→      \"evidence\": [\n    51→        {\n    52→          \"statement\": \"Prince Prospero reacts with extreme rage and demands execution of the masked figure\",\n    53→          \"quote\": \"Seize him and unmask him -- that we may know whom we have to hang at sunrise, from the battlements!\",\n    54→          \"position\": 11148,\n    55→          \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    56→        },\n    57→        {\n    58→          \"statement\": \"He is physically bold and authoritative, commanding the attention of the assembled revellers\",\n    59→          \"quote\": \"It was in the eastern or blue chamber