read of the 'Red Death,' a horrific plague marked by bleeding pores and rapid death, prompting Prince Prospero to retreat with a thousand courtiers into a secluded, fortified abbey to escape contagion. Inside, he constructs seven elaborately themed rooms—each with uniquely colored stained-glass windows and decor—culminating in a black chamber with blood-red panes and a massive ebony clock that chimes hourly, halting all merriment and instilling dread. During a lavish masked ball, a mysterious figure appears dressed as the Red Death itself, shrouded in grave-cloths and drenched in scarlet stains, causing terror and paralysis among the guests. Prince Prospero, enraged by the blasphemy, pursues the figure through all seven rooms with a dagger, only to collapse and die upon confronting it in the black chamber, where the figure is revealed to be an empty shell. As the prince dies, the plague manifests among the revelers, and one by one they perish, extinguishing the lights and silence falling over the abbey as death claims all.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"characters\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"char_the_prince_prospero_d85685e9\",\n      \"canonical_name\": \"the Prince Prospero\",\n      \"aliases\": [\n        \"the mummer\"\n      ],\n      \"role\": null,\n      \"appearance\": null,\n      \"personality\": null,\n      \"voice_guidance\": null,\n      \"descriptions\": [\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Prince Prospero is a tyrannical and self-indulgent ruler who responds to perceived threats with violent rage and authoritarian control. His actions escalate from arrogance and cruelty to panic and futile aggression, culminating in his own death at the hands of the very symbol of the plague he sought to deny. His behavior reveals a deep-seated fear of mortality and a willingness to sacrifice others to maintain power and illusion.\",\n          \"source_position\": 10339,\n          \"chapter_index\": null,\n          \"confidence\": \"llm_refined\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"relationships\": {},\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"statement\": \"Prince Prospero reacts with extreme rage and demands execution of the masked figure\",\n          \"quote\": \"Seize him and unmask him -- that we may know whom we have to hang at sunrise, from the battlements!\",\n          \"position\": 11148,\n          \"confidence\": \"high\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"statement\": \"He is physically bold and authoritative, commanding the attention of the assembled revellers\",\n          \"quote\": \"It was in the eastern or blue chamber in which stood the Prince Prospero as he uttered these words. They rang throughout the seven rooms loudly and clearly -- for the prince was a bold and robust man, and the music had become hushed at the waving of...\",\n          \"position\": 11148,\n          \"confidence\": \"high\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"statement\": \"He pursues the masked figure with fury after being humiliated by his presence\",\n          \"quote\": \"It was then, however, that the Prince Prospero, maddening with rage and the shame of his own momentary cowardice, rushed hurriedly through the six chambers, while none followed him on account of a deadly terror that had...\",\n          \"position\": 12389,\n          \"confidence\": \"high\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"statement\": \"He is fatally stabbed by the masked figure, who is revealed to be the Red Death\",\n          \"quote\": \"There was a sharp cry -- and the dagger dropped gleaming upon the sable carpet, upon which, instantly afterwards, fell prostrate in death the Prince Prospero.\",\n          \"position\": 12980,\n          \"confidence\": \"high\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"statement\": \"The masked figure is revealed to be wearing grave clothes and a corpse-like mask, symbolizing the Red Death\",\n          \"quote\": \"gasped in unutterable horror at finding the grave cerements and corpse-like mask which they handled...\",\n     