ered by the grotesque intrusion. Prince Prospero, furious at the sacrilege and the disruption of his illusion of control, draws a dagger and pursues the figure through the seven rooms, each one symbolizing a stage of life and decay. His pursuit is both a physical and symbolic journey, reflecting his futile attempt to defy death and maintain his power and privilege.\n\nThe climax unfolds in the black chamber, where the figure is revealed to be an empty shell—no living person, but a manifestation of the very plague they sought to escape. Prince Prospero collapses and dies instantly, his arrogance and denial finally undone. In that moment, the Red Death manifests among the revelers: one by one, they fall, their bodies succumbing to the same symptoms that ravaged the world outside. The lights go out, the music ceases, and silence descends as the abbey is claimed by death. The story ends with the complete annihilation of the isolated elite, underscoring the inevitability of mortality and the futility of attempting to escape it through wealth, power, or isolation.</div>\n                \n                <p style=\"margin-top: 1rem; color: var(--muted);\">\n                    <strong>Themes:</strong> identity, ambition, loss\n                </p>\n                \n            </section>\n            \n\n            \n            <section>\n                <h2>🤖 Analysis Models</h2>\n                <table style=\"width: 100%; margin-top: 1rem; border-collapse: collapse;\">\n                    <thead>\n                        <tr style=\"border-bottom: 2px solid var(--primary);\">\n                            <th style=\"text-align: left; padding: 0.75rem; color: var(--muted);\">Phase</th>\n                            <th style=\"text-align: left; padding: 0.75rem; color: var(--muted);\">Model</th>\n                            <th style=\"text-align: left; padding: 0.75rem; color: var(--muted);\">Provider</th>\n                        </tr>\n                    </thead>